\section{The Unit-Disk Maximum Independent Set problem}\label{sec:udmis_theory}

The \emph{Unit-Disk}
MIS (UD-MIS) problem is the MIS problem restricted to \emph{unit-disk graphs}.
A graph is a unit-disk graph if one can associate a position in the 2D plane to every vertex such that two vertices share an edge if and only if their distance is smaller than unity.
Figure~\ref{fig:ud_graph} displays an example of a unit-disk graph, with an example maximum independent set for that graph, in red.


