In this section, we derive an approximate upper bound for the expectation value of the maximum of the approximation ratio computed over $N$ samples of a \emph{uniform} distribution of states,
\begin{equation}
    p_i = \frac{1}{d}, \;\forall i = 0 \dots d-1
\end{equation}
with $d=2^S$, and $S$ denotes the system size ($S = N_\mathrm{atoms}$ and $N=n_\mathrm{shots}$ in the main text).

The cost function we consider for a solution (bitstring) $i=(n^i_1, \dots, n^i_S)$ is its Hamming weight (sum of bits):

\begin{equation}
E_i(S) = \sum_{k = 1}^{S} n^i_k
\end{equation}

